<div class="modal fade" id="notebook-help-modal" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="notebook-help-title" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-scrollable modal-fullscreen-sm-down">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h2 class="modal-title fs-5" id="notebook-help-title">Taking notes</h2>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close help"></button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold">Start a note</h3>
        <ol>
          <li>Sign in and connect your Google Drive from <a href="<%= utils.urlFor(req, '/settings') %>">My Settings</a>. Your notes are saved as Markdown files in your own Drive.</li>
          <li>Select <strong>New note</strong> in My Notebook to create a general note, or select the <i class="bi bi-sticky" aria-hidden="true"></i> note icon beside a hadith, Quran ayah, or tafsir.</li>
          <li>Give the note a title that is different from your other note titles, then write your note. Changes save automatically after you pause typing; use the checkmark to save and preview.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Use the eye/pencil control to switch between preview and editing. Click the title or tags to edit them; they collapse when you return to the note body. Add tags separated by spaces, or write hashtags such as <code>#reflection</code> in your note. Use search and tag filters to find notes later.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Keep a note open while reading</h3>
        <p>Select the pin icon in a note's header to float it beside the page. The minus icon minimizes it to a <strong>Restore note</strong> button. You can scroll and browse the site while it stays available; the saved note reopens as you move between pages in the same tab. Select the pin again to return to the regular dialog, or close the note to stop following it.</p>
        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Markdown basics</h3>
        <p>Type these examples in the editor. Formatting appears in preview.</p>
        <div class="table-responsive">
          <table class="table table-sm align-middle">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Formatting</th><th scope="col">What to type</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Headings</th><td><code># Main heading</code><br><code>## Section heading</code><br><code>### Smaller heading</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Emphasis</th><td><code>**bold**</code>, <code>*italic*</code>, <code>~~strikethrough~~</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Lists</th><td><code>- A bullet point</code><br><code>1. A numbered point</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Quotation</th><td><code>&gt; Quoted text</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Link</th><td><code>[Link text](https://example.com)</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Inline code</th><td><code>`literal text`</code></td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Divider</th><td><code>---</code> on its own line</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p>Leave a blank line between paragraphs. Arabic and English can be used together; text direction adjusts automatically.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Link your notes</h3>
        <p>Type <code>[[</code> followed by at least two letters from a note title to see suggestions. Matching ignores case and diacritics and can find words anywhere in a title.</p>
        <p><code>[[The Mahdi]]</code> links to that note. Use <code>[[The Mahdi|my research]]</code> to display a different label. Note links and ordinary web links open in a new tab.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Expand a reference</h3>
        <p>Type a plain reference such as <code>bukhari:1</code>, <code>quran:1:1</code>, or <code>quran:17:18-20</code>. In preview, select its <i class="bi bi-arrows-angle-expand" aria-hidden="true"></i> expand icon to replace it with the Arabic text, English translation, and source citation. Quran ranges include each ayah in order, in ordinary Arabic script.</p>
        <p>The expand icon is not shown for references inside an explicit Markdown link or code.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Footnotes</h3>
        <p>Put the reference in your text and its definition on a separate line:</p>
        <pre class="bg-body-tertiary rounded p-3"><code>A point worth explaining.[^1]

[^1]: The explanation goes here.</code></pre>
        <p>Arabic digits work too: <code>[^١]</code> with <code>[^١]: Explanation</code>. References keep the digits you typed; the footnote list uses English digits.</p>

        <h3 class="fs-6 fw-bold mt-4">Download your notes</h3>
        <p>The download icon inside a note saves that note as a Markdown file. The download icon on My Notebook saves your notebook as a ZIP file.</p>
        <p class="mb-0">Select the printer icon inside a note to print its formatted text, title, source, and tags, including your latest edits. Choose <strong>Save as PDF</strong> in the print dialog to download a PDF, or select your printer for a paper copy.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-primary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Got it</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
